      {#- Outcome-based services (founder, 2026-11-25). Ticketing is the first
          and it is under construction with design partners: never describe it
          as shipped, and give no prices until the founder sets them. -#}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="outcome-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="outcome-h">Outcome-based services</h2>
        <h3 class="ent-h">Some work is better paid for by the result.</h3>
        <p class="ent-body">With an outcome-based service you pay for the work done, like a ticket resolved, instead of for the agent by the month. Ticketing comes first. You assign specific agents to specific types of questions, and you can spin up a new type of question, or a whole new support process, straight from a collaborative project. The questions, the agents, the approvals and the reporting all live in one place.</p>
        <p class="ent-callout"><b>Under construction.</b> We are building outcome-based services with design partners and they are not generally available yet. Ticketing is first, and other support and back-office processes will follow the same way.</p>
        <p class="ent-body">Want to see if an outcome-based setup fits your team? Email <a href="mailto:{{ contact }}?subject={{ 'Outcome-based services: OpenShore' | urlencode }}">{{ contact }}</a> and we will work out whether we can set one up with you. <a href="/pricing/">How it is priced</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="workers-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="workers-h">Agents</h2>
        <p class="ent-body"><b>Agents</b> are built by domain experts and run whole corporate functions. Each one is its own harness inside the OpenShore Harness, so it stays contained and works to the standards of quality and security OpenShore holds every agent to, whatever model runs it. Each agent is assigned an admin on your team who approves what matters. The Finance agent, for one, drafts your monthly board pack and investor update from your own numbers. Pick from the five, or we build the one you need. All of them work from Data Foundations, the layer that brings your connected apps into one set of numbers. <a href="/#bots-h">Watch each one work</a>.</p>
        <ul class="ent-pills ent-pills--workers" role="list"><li>Sales ops</li><li>Finance</li><li>Planning</li><li>Supply chain</li><li>Analytics</li></ul>
      </section>

{#- The worked examples play on the home page only (founder, 2026-11-24:
    all five moved there, so the tour no longer repeats them). -#}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="trust-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="trust-h">Built to be trusted</h2>
        <ul class="ent-checks" role="list">
          <li>Any model, cloud or local, on your keys, in your cloud or on your own servers, with no lock-in. Our harnesses lessen each model’s volatility, so agents stay steady whichever you run.</li>
          <li>Agents propose. People approve anything that touches money, records or outbound messages.</li>
          <li>Every number traces to its source, calculated by code, never by the model.</li>
          <li>Each person sees only what they’re allowed to. No one sees another person’s pay or quota.</li>
          <li>Privacy first: we never sell your data or use it to train AI models. By default we see service telemetry, like errors and uptime, with no customer content; anything deeper is with your permission, limited to that task, and logged.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

